 "boundary_note": "Fought on new ward boundaries following the LGBCE electoral review of Blackpool (final recommendations 2022), implemented by The Blackpool (Electoral Changes) Order 2022 (made 20 December 2022) and first used at this election: 42 councillors across 21 two-councillor wards; most ward boundaries changed, six unchanged, and the ward names were retained from the previous pattern.",
 "notes": [
  "All 21 wards sourced from Blackpool Council's own declared results: the blackpool.gov.uk 2023 results page is rendered from the council's public Google Sheet (ID 17DgoWA5P3C8WygKW1jmMFngjDx_gzDDA-aLpbxMEOoc, referenced in the page's run-council-elections.js); every figure above was read directly from that sheet.",
  "Independently cross-checked against Andrew Teale's LEAP (andrewteale.me.uk/leap/results/2023/83/): every vote count in every ward matches the council sheet exactly.",
  "Cross-checked against Democracy Club ballot pages (candidates.democracyclub.org.uk/elections/local.blackpool.<ward>.2023-05-04/, all locked against SOPNs, result source = the council page): DC matches except two DC transcription errors, Waterloo Tina Louise Rothery 150 (council/LEAP/Wikipedia: 170) and Bloomfield electorate 4453 (council: 4553).",
  "Wikipedia's article has one vote-count typo: Layton, Roy Henry Haskett 353 (council/LEAP/DC: 352); Wikipedia also misspells Therese Bernadette Clark (Anchorsholme) as 'Theresa'.",
  "Candidate names are as declared by the council (full names as nominated); DC SOPN-verified names agree.",
  "Turnout figures are the council's own (verified ballot papers / electorate); DC pages round to whole percentages.",
